 "help": "usage: wgsextract vcf gatk [-h] [-r REGION] [--scatter] [--gpu] [--pair-hmm-cuda PAIR_HMM_CUDA]\n                           [--pair-hmm-neon PAIR_HMM_NEON] [--reference-evidence {none,gvcf}]\n                           [--help-all]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  -r, --region REGION   Chromosomal region (e.g. chrM)\n  --scatter             Opt-in Ultima flow-mode interval scattering, bounded by --threads and\n                        available RAM (6 GiB per worker, 4 GiB Java heap). Can change\n                        genotypes/annotations away from interval boundaries; default: one\n                        unscattered process.\n  --gpu                 Call on an NVIDIA GPU with Parabricks (Linux, Docker; see\n                        docs/hardware.md#nvidia-gpus-parabricks).\n  --pair-hmm-cuda PAIR_HMM_CUDA\n                        Experimental Linux x86-64 CUDA PairHMM sidecar jar for GATK 4.6.2.0, with\n                        GKL CPU fallback. Opt-in; not Parabricks. See native/pairhmm/README.md.\n                        Not with --gpu or --scatter.\n  --pair-hmm-neon PAIR_HMM_NEON\n                        Experimental Apple Silicon double-precision NEON PairHMM sidecar jar for\n                        GATK 4.6.2.0, with Java fallback. Opt-in; not Parabricks. See\n                        packaging/arm64/gkl/README.md. Not with --gpu or --scatter.\n  --reference-evidence {none,gvcf}\n                        Also write reference evidence: a gVCF, gatk.g.vcf.gz (+ .tbi), beside the\n                        unchanged variant VCF (gvcf; costs little time; the VCF is then genotyped\n                        from it; not with --gpu or --scatter), or not (none). Default: config\n                        reference_evidence, else none.\n  --help-all            Show this help with the advanced options too, and exit.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\n2 advanced options not shown; 'wgsextract vcf gatk --help-all' lists them.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract vcf gatk --input sample.cram\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  gatk.vcf.gz (+ .tbi).\n\nneeds:\n  gatk, samtools, tabix; depending on options and inputs, also: bcftools;\n  hours on a 30x genome.\n",
